  "notes": [
   "Each of the 12 LED blocks connects one Mega PWM pin (2-13, copy n -> pin n+1) through a 220 ohm resistor to an LED anode; cathodes go via a black jumper to the shared ground rail, which is wired to Mega GND.",
   "Exact breadboard columns are chosen for a clean layout (copy n uses column 2n-1 for resistor/anode and column 2n for cathode); the image spaces them irregularly but the connectivity is the same.",
   "The breadboard is oriented per the catalogue: bank 't' rows a-e, bank 'b' rows f-j; resistors straddle the centre gap. Ground rail 'tn.1' is one strip.",
   "The Mega GND port is assumed to be named 'GND.1' (catalogue port list truncated).",
   "The anode is the longer LED leg; in the image the LED leg next to the resistor column is the anode, the other is the cathode.",
   "Resistor value 220 ohm per the manual; the image resistor band colours were not used."
  ]
 },
